                    104.0,
                    185.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. Employees shall not be permitted to secure, through bidding, the same consecutive days off, on the same shift more than two (2) times annually. Employees hired in between bid periods will be assigned by the Agency. Employees who successfully bid or are assigned to a Flex position shall secure a shift and days off work schedule through the bid process and shall revert back to the shift and days off when not assigned by the Agency to relieve other security employees. (The intent of this Section is that employees who successfully bid or is assigned to a Flex Variable Position will primarily provide relief to other security employees on the shift the position is assigned to.)",
            "block_bbox": [
                104,
                185,
                1118,
                361
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    104.0,
                    185.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    185.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    361.0
                ],
                [
                    104.0,
                    361.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "5. Bidding shall occur every four (4) as months becoming effective on the second Sunday of March, July and November. The parties agree to meet and confer if a six (6)-month rotation system is being considered.",
            "block_bbox": [
                105,
                363,
                1118,
                437
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    105.0,
                    363.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    363.0
                ],
                [
                    1118.0,
                    437.0
                ],
                [
                    105.0,
                    437.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "6. During each bid rotation period, the Agency will identify certain work schedules for employees assigned as inmate work crew supervisors that may be assigned to rotate five (5) shifts of eight (8) hours and two (2) consecutive days off within each workweek, or four (4) shifts of ten (10) hours and three (3) days off. Employees assigned as work crew supervisors may volunteer for these alternate schedules at the time of the bid on the bid sheet in order to help carry out the inmate work program mission of the Agency. The Agency shall first assign employees who are assigned as work crew supervisors and who volunteer to change their work schedule between a 5-8 work schedule and a 4-10 work schedule before a change in schedule is made. If there are not sufficient employees who volunteer to move between these schedules during the bid period as needed by the Agency in carrying out its inmate work program mission, employees assigned to these duties may be assigned to a 4-10 schedule in reverse seniority order for a period of time during the bid as needed to carry out the work program needs of the Agency. The Agency will revert any affected employee(s) back to their bid shift and days off work schedule when the employee has completed the 4-10 work schedule assignment. Employees will be given seven (7) days written notice of change in schedule.",
            "block_bbox": [
                104,
                437,
                1118,
                790
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
